    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:fb5db666cae6efb7",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "8cdd7addb0966090be207c183e8ed7038ffa8dd2b4bc53a63c25d26905161544",
      "text": "Sail to the Maroon village of Nieuw-Aurora for a walk past the mission post, church, school and medical post, and hear about the Maroons, descendants of Africans who escaped slavery, and their traditions; walk in the island’s forest to learn about medicinal plants, with dinner and a cultural dance performance in the evening (minimum 8 guests). The next morning, swim, walk or revisit the village before lunch, then return by boat to Atjoni and by bus to Paramaribo.",
